===================== Done =========================================

Windows support (partially done)

Windows watcher agent is built — needs production testing across Windows 7, 10, 11, Server 2019, 2022
Windows-specific correlation rules (brute force on 4625, lateral movement on 4648, privilege escalation on 4672)
Windows-specific artifact seeds matching Event ID patterns

-------------------------------------------------------------------

========================== In Progress ============================


Correlation engine improvements

Time-window enforcement — the time_window_seconds parameter exists in the code but is not actually enforced. A 5-step rule should only fire if all steps arrive within the configured window, not just if they all appear eventually
Entity-field grouping by username — rules like "same user failed on server A then succeeded on server B" require grouping by user not just IP. The entity_field column exists in use_cases but the engine always groups by IP
Threshold-based rules — "if the same IP triggers more than N hits in M seconds" without requiring a specific sequence. Currently requires a workaround
Rule hit cooldown — prevent the same rule from firing repeatedly within a configurable window
True sequence ordering enforcement — the order flag does a lenient presence check, not a real timestamp-ordered sequence check
Correlation across multiple source IPs for detecting distributed attacks

-----------------------------------------------------------------

=========================== TO DO ================================

Log collection

Agent health alerting — raise an alarm when a watcher stops sending heartbeats for more than N minutes. Currently a silent watcher is only visible on the Clients page
Log rotation handling — if a log file is rotated while the watcher is running, the offset tracking can miss lines or re-read them
UDP reliability improvements — the UDP path has no acknowledgement or retry

Parser gaps

Zeek/Bro network IDS (conn.log, dns.log, http.log, ssl.log)
Suricata/Snort IDS alerts
AWS CloudTrail
Windows Sysmon (XML format — extremely rich telemetry)
Palo Alto, Fortinet, Cisco ASA dedicated parsers (syslog parser handles these partially)
Version 2 — Features discussed but not yet built

Alert management

Alert escalation workflow — assign an alert to a specific analyst, set a status (open / investigating / resolved), add timestamped notes
Alert suppression rules — suppress alerts matching a pattern for N hours during planned maintenance
Email alerts fully working — SMTP is wired but email sends are failing in production

Search and filtering

Advanced search on the Logs page — proper filters for IP, hostname, action, severity, date range, logical operators (AND/OR/NOT). Currently just a string match across the whole database
Saved searches — bookmark frequently used queries

Reporting

Scheduled PDF reports — automatically generate and email a weekly report
Custom date range in reports — currently only preset periods
MTTA trending chart — show how mean time to acknowledge is changing over time
Compliance report templates mapped to ISO 27001, SOC 2, NIST CSF

User management

Two-factor authentication (TOTP)
Per-user dashboard customisation — choose which widgets appear and their order
Full audit log for user actions across the platform — not just archive operations

Dashboard

Mobile-responsive layout — current grid breaks below 768px
Dark/light theme toggle
More widget types — top talkers, geographic IP map, events per parser
Version 2 — Infrastructure

Installer

Single install.sh that sets up PostgreSQL, creates the schema, installs Python dependencies, configures Apache/Nginx, creates systemd units, generates TLS certs, and seeds the database. Currently all steps are manual.

systemd service files

Proper unit files for opensiem.py, spector_state_observer.py, and malicious_keywords_updater.py with restart policies, logging to journald, and automatic startup on boot

PostgreSQL connection pooling

Every PHP request opens and closes its own connection. PgBouncer in front of PostgreSQL would handle load much better at scale

Log archival integration (partially done)

Archive search needs the date-picker UI instead of the browser prompt() for Run Archive Now
Rehydration needs more testing on large date ranges
Archive search page needs the DuckDB CLI confirmed working end-to-end on the server
Version 3 — Longer horizon

Threat intelligence

STIX/TAXII feed support — standard threat intelligence exchange format
IP reputation lookup on alert — when an alert fires from an external IP, automatically query AbuseIPDB or VirusTotal and attach the result to the alert
IOC expiry and review workflow — mark artifacts as review pending after a configurable age

Scale and reliability

Multi-node support — secondary node for the correlation engine and a shared DB for basic HA
PostgreSQL log archival to cold storage — messages older than 90 days moved to a compressed archive table keeping the main Message table fast (archive system now handles this)
TLS mutual authentication — client certificates on watchers so the server can verify which agent is connecting

CI/CD (partially documented)

Full GitHub Actions pipeline as designed in the DevOps guide
Docker packaging for those who want containerised deployment
Automated integration tests against a real PostgreSQL instance

Compliance and legal

Legal hold interface improvements — bulk freeze, freeze expiry dates, freeze audit trail
Compliance report export in formats required by specific frameworks

IOC management

Automatic feed health monitoring — alert if a configured IOC feed URL returns an error or hasn't updated in 48 hours
Multi-backend archive replication — write to local path AND S3 simultaneously for redundancy
